00:24:04,208 --> 00:24:08,612
So our research focuses on the co-design of complicated systems.

186
00:24:09,198 --> 00:24:17,220
And our perspective is to provide a correct, in some sense, abstraction of system design framework for complicated systems.

187
00:24:17,646 --> 00:24:20,036
So what do we mean by correct abstraction here?

188
00:24:20,288 --> 00:24:28,324
We mean the abstraction or the mathematical framework should be able to cover the things that we actually care about in the real world about complicated systems.

189
00:24:28,590 --> 00:24:33,956
So the thing that they can provide, the thing that they require, and the options available for them.

190
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:39,492
And we require the abstraction to be compositional, computational, and collaborative.

191
00:24:40,750 --> 00:24:41,888
What do we mean by compositional?

192
00:24:41,968 --> 00:24:55,204
It means that we have to be able to synthesize the analysis and the results from lower-level systems, say the sensors, the autonomous vehicles themselves, to higher-level performance systems, say the mobility system of a city.

193
00:24:55,808 --> 00:24:59,568
So deriving from this compositionality, we need collaborative.

194
00:24:59,968 --> 00:25:09,444
So different people or different domain experts should be able to contribute to different components, kind of independently of how other components contribute to the system.

195
00:25:10,128 --> 00:25:17,700
And we also require it to be competitionally tractable for obvious reasons, otherwise, we will not be able to use this framework in practice.

196
00:25:18,414 --> 00:25:27,248
So that's an overview of a co-design framework that we believe should be correct in this sense the abstraction of system co-design.

