00:31:06,638 --> 00:31:10,368
There is no further structure, no layered architecture.

245
00:31:10,830 --> 00:31:19,568
People in Ara also talk about the need for hierarchy, the need for time abstraction, action abstraction, all of these things.

246
00:31:20,142 --> 00:31:22,372
In current arguments, this is not happening.

247
00:31:23,054 --> 00:31:28,208
In the control literature, I see people are keep talking about the layered architectures.

248
00:31:28,288 --> 00:31:29,248
I really like that.

249
00:31:29,408 --> 00:31:42,928
I just wish we knew how to bring that formalism to RL to create these systems that should be much better, should be much more capable of dealing with long horizon problems.

250
00:31:43,534 --> 00:31:47,652
Also, current RL is model free, mostly.

251
00:31:48,270 --> 00:31:53,316
If you look at the algorithms that people actually use, they're mainly model free.

252
00:31:53,648 --> 00:31:55,648
But clearly that cannot be the case.

253
00:31:55,808 --> 00:32:02,688
Like we should have the model, like it's not like that people don't work on model based algorithms, people do work on model based algorithms.

