00:32:58,976 --> 00:33:05,252
So I for sure know that we have to do other things, but it's a little bit unclear how.

270
00:33:06,926 --> 00:33:11,364
Lastly, RL is about reward and reward maximization.

271
00:33:11,950 --> 00:33:13,776
And that feels very off as well.

272
00:33:14,496 --> 00:33:21,376
Because I don't think that reward should be maximized, you know, like under all circumstances.

273
00:33:21,616 --> 00:33:29,536
It feels more like homeostasis is the right way of talking about how to build systems that are robust and capable.

274
00:33:29,776 --> 00:33:35,296
And I always do this that RL is just maximizing rewards.

275
00:33:35,376 --> 00:33:36,816
It's like a first approximation.

276
00:33:36,896 --> 00:33:38,656
And it's like it's a good starting point.

277
00:33:38,976 --> 00:33:49,616
But maybe it's time to take it a little bit more seriously because the reward maximization might actually be holding us back because we are too hung up on it.

278
00:33:49,696 --> 00:33:58,176
And maybe there are, you know, like there is life, there is easier algorithms that are not maximizing the reward, but just you know, keeping homeostasis.

279
00:33:58,256 --> 00:33:59,616
Uh all right.

